    "created_at": "2024-03-01T17:18:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-01T17:19:18Z",
    "body": "> Is there an option in GA not to gather any personal data? The website might also need some kind of consent prompt.\r\n\r\nNo. GA implies giving data (URL, browser's user agent, IP address, …) to a third party (Google). Giving data to a third party¹ without getting user consent before is forbidden by GDPR for any website served to the European Union.\r\n\r\nIn other words, any alternative must be self-hosted or only enabled after asking the user with those ugly cookie prompts.\r\n\r\n_____\r\n¹ there are some exceptions I think, but they don't apply here. Also: I am not a lawyer, so don't take for granted what I wrote.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
